      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T06:39:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need this and a std::optional for the advertising_set_id?\n\nIt feels like the advertising_set_id should always be populated if we\u0027re peripheral, and never populated if we\u0027re Central.\n\nCan we simplify it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5c7ca734636d0e2196551c9ca65f4b7f9f4fc32a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57755e1b_2f668ed7",
        "filename": "system/gd/hci/acl_manager/le_acl_connection.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T02:19:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The std::optional is needed for legacy advertising, since then we don\u0027t have a set ID.\n\nThis case is needed when we store the connection inside le_impl before sending it upwards. Constructing the connection later is possible but messy since we\u0027d need to store all the parameters + the queue in another struct, so I thought the simpler way is to just have a variant that is never realized after we return upwards.",
      "parentUuid": "ab2a5700_6c7fc1f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5c7ca734636d0e2196551c9ca65f4b7f9f4fc32a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
